From d534eff26ba52976905c98241e6038228ac95fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneplus-nord2t-karen contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 03:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] build: raise Gradle daemon memory

The Vector Android build exhausts and thrashes the default 512 MiB Gradle
daemon heap while resolving and compiling the native module. Put the JVM
arguments in Gradle's properties file so the complete space-separated value
reaches the daemon as one property in both dependency and offline builds.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
---
 gradle.properties | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gradle.properties b/gradle.properties
index 941da43..95abc8d 100644
--- a/gradle.properties
+++ b/gradle.properties
@@ -14 +14,2 @@
-android.useAndroidX=true
+org.gradle.jvmargs=-Xmx4g -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=1g -Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
+android.useAndroidX=true
